00:00:13.869 --> 00:00:18.439
STUDENT: I was just curious if we took Ates's discussion of secular--

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:21.039
anthropology of secularism? Maybe that secularism is not 

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:23.580
just a principle, but is

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.639
in some kind of formation of cultures and beliefs,

00:00:26.639 --> 00:00:29.499
and apply that concept to Professor Gorski's 

00:00:29.499 --> 00:00:31.139
categories of missionary strategies,

00:00:31.139 --> 00:00:34.180
parachurch organizations-- would secularism 

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.639
not still have a chance to itself have

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:41.100
the ability to apply those kinds of strategies, build up those kinds of

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.540
organizations

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.100
at the appropriate secular states' relations and

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.680
still, perhaps, be able to adapt in the same ways, and maybe make its own resurgence?

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.300
GORSKI: It could.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.750
You know, I mean, they'd need to invent a new ideology, because the two big

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.640
versions of that, which were

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.600
fascism and Communism

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.250
are basically, you know, for all--

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.140
as far as we know, extinct. I mention them because those are--

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.390
you know, those are-- those are movements which really did build,

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:12.660
you know, a complex ritual life,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:18.220
a kind of fully developed cosmology of one kind or another,

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.610
extensive networks of--

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.030
of various kinds of

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:28.180
"parachurch organizations"-- you know, papers, et cetera et cetera
et cetera.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:33.010
Interestingly, to some degree in response to-- in response to and interaction

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:33.390
with

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.230
particularly Catholic

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.180
kind of confessional movements 

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.970
during the nineteenth century.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:41.940
There's a lot of interplay and interaction

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.680
between those two,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.909
and interestingly,

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:49.369
some of the few places where you actually find Protestants replicating that are

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:52.799
places where they are in direct competition

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:55.340
with both Catholic

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.240
and kind of socialist--

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.370
socialist movements. Netherlands is the classic
example of this, but 

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.850
you find this

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:02.610
also, to

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.450
some extent, in Austria,

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:06.979
Belgium to a

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:08.119
lesser degree,

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:10.079
some parts of Germany.

00:02:10.079 --> 00:02:12.869
ALTINORDU: And I think there are

00:02:12.869 --> 00:02:14.560
actually these organizations. I mean

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.690
that in Turkey, definitely there's this attempt to 

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.499
organize against Islamists, that there's also, you know,

00:02:19.499 --> 00:02:22.620
a foundation to support modern life. That's one, for example,

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.729
that's a kind of--

00:02:23.729 --> 00:02:27.209
has also charity functions, but definitely they want to propagate, defend

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:29.020
secularism against a kind of 

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.169
re-Islamization of 

00:02:31.169 --> 00:02:32.299
public life in Turkey.

00:02:32.299 --> 00:02:34.739
I think in Germany, too-- lots of

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:35.859
kind of

00:02:35.859 --> 00:02:40.519
immigrant organizations that are based in Turkey
are actually 

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:42.750
nationalist and secular, and they did actually

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.160
experience lots of tension

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.919
with the Islamist organizations as they competed

00:02:46.919 --> 00:02:49.699
over immigrants

00:02:49.699 --> 00:02:51.619
to provide their primary

00:02:51.619 --> 00:02:52.289
organizations,

00:02:52.289 --> 00:02:55.209
although now that tension has ceased, and

00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:58.169
in the German context, the Islamic 

00:02:58.169 --> 00:03:01.340
organizations were much more successful.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:05.160
Because they were also organized around mosque communities, whereas the other

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.699
organizations didn't have this kind of--

00:03:06.699 --> 00:03:10.090
I mean, the religion provides a very kind of

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.119
ready-made language 

00:03:12.119 --> 00:03:13.999
for these organizations

00:03:13.999 --> 00:03:15.409
that enables them to 

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:16.589
much easily,

00:03:16.589 --> 00:03:19.539
much easier attract

00:03:19.539 --> 00:03:21.829
immigrants versus let's say

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:23.750
some of these other alternative organizations who are,

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.159
let's say, Socialists, and--

00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:27.529
so they didn't have the same kind of 

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:30.150
connection to the-- to kind of cultural

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.129
idioms and 

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:32.550
language that this kind of 

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.209
religious communal language.

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:36.159
And actually the--

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:38.080
these secular organizations gave up, because

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.359
they saw that they needed to collaborate with 

00:03:40.359 --> 00:03:42.420
the Islamic organizations if they want to

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.529
claim any kind of

00:03:43.529 --> 00:03:45.239
